.TH elfshaker-find 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-find \- Search snapshot tags in known pack indexes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker find\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITERM\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints snapshots whose tags contain TERM as a case\-sensitive substring, together with the pack containing each snapshot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fITERM\fR> [default: ]
Case\-sensitive substring to find in snapshot tags.
